#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:6
msgid "Migrating your package.xml to format 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:12
msgid ""
"ROS 2 requires ``package.xml`` files to use at least `format 2 <https://reps."
"openrobotics.org/rep-0140/>`__. This guide shows how to migrate a ``package."
"xml`` from format 1 to format 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:15
msgid ""
"If the ``<package>`` tag at the start of your ``package.xml`` looks like "
"either of the following, then it is using format 1 and you must migrate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:17
msgid "<package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:21
msgid "<package format=\"1\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:27
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:29
msgid ""
"You should have a working ROS 1 installation. This enables you to check that "
"the converted ``package.xml`` is valid by building and testing the package, "
"since ROS 1 supports all ``package.xml`` format versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:33
msgid "Migrate from format 1 to 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:35
msgid ""
"Format 1 and format 2 differ in how they specify dependencies. Read the "
"`compatibility section in REP-0140 <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-0140/"
"#compatibility>`__ for a summary of the differences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:39
msgid "Add ``format`` attribute to ``<package>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:41
msgid ""
"Add or set the ``format`` attribute to ``2`` to indicate that the ``package."
"xml`` uses format 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:43
msgid "<package format=\"2\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:48
msgid "Replace ``<run_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:50
msgid ""
"The ``<run_depend>`` tag is no longer allowed. If you have a dependency "
"specified like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:53
msgid "<run_depend>foo</run_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:57
msgid "then replace it with one or both of these tags:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:59
msgid ""
"<build_export_depend>foo</build_export_depend>\n"
"<exec_depend>foo</exec_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:64
msgid ""
"If the dependency is needed when something in your package is executed, then "
"use the ``<exec_depend>`` tag. If packages that depend on your package need "
"the dependency when they are built, then use the ``<build_export_depend>`` "
"tag. Use both tags if you are unsure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:69
msgid "Convert some ``<build_depend>`` to ``<test_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:71
msgid ""
"In format 1 ``<test_depend>`` declares dependencies that are needed when "
"running your package's tests. It still does that in format 2, but it "
"additionally declares dependencies that are needed when building your "
"package's tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:74
msgid ""
"Because of the limitations of this tag in format 1, your package may have a "
"test-only dependency specified as a ``<build_depend>`` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:76
msgid "<build_depend>testfoo</build_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:80
msgid "If so, change it to a ``<test_depend>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:82
msgid "<test_depend>testfoo</test_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:88
msgid ""
"If you are using CMake, then make sure your test dependencies are only "
"referenced within a ``if(BUILD_TESTING)`` block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:90
msgid ""
"if (BUILD_TESTING)\n"
"    find_package(testfoo REQUIRED)\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:97
msgid "Begin using ``<doc_depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:99
msgid ""
"Use the new ``<doc_depend>`` tag to declare dependencies needed for building "
"your package's documentation. For example, C++ packages might have this "
"dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:102
msgid "<doc_depend>doxygen</doc_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:106
msgid "while Python packages might have this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:108
msgid "<doc_depend>python3-sphinx</doc_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:112
msgid ""
"See :doc:`the guide on documenting ROS 2 packages <../../Developer-Tools/"
"Package-documentation/Documenting-a-ROS-2-Package>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:115
msgid "Simplify dependencies with ``<depend>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:117
msgid ""
"``<depend>`` is a new tag that makes ``package.xml`` files more concise. If "
"your ``package.xml`` has these three tags for the same dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:120
msgid ""
"<build_depend>foo</build_depend>\n"
"<build_export_depend>foo</build_export_depend>\n"
"<exec_depend>foo</exec_depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:126
msgid "then replace them with a single ``<depend>`` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:128
msgid "<depend>foo</depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:133
msgid "Test your new ``package.xml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Migration-and-Upgrades/Migrating-from-ROS1/Migrating-Package-XML.rst:135
msgid ""
"Build and test your package as you normally do using ``catkin_make``, "
"``cakin_make_isolated``, or the ``catkin`` build tool. If everything "
"succeeds, then your ``package.xml`` is valid."
msgstr ""
